minixml: parseelt: check the end of the buffer before looking for a closing tag

After element data, parseelt() reads the byte that follows '<' to see whether
a closing tag starts. When that '<' is the last byte of the buffer, the read
is one byte past the heap buffer.

Upstream commit 42965d7e763b4f894986dd8feb19db7920ea0766, made after
miniupnpc 2.3.3.

--- a/src/minixml.c
+++ b/src/minixml.c
@@ -197,7 +197,7 @@
 							if ((p->xml + 1) >= p->xmlend)
 								return;
 						}
-						if(i>0 && p->datafunc && *(p->xml + 1) == '/')
+						if(i>0 && p->datafunc && (p->xml + 1) < p->xmlend && *(p->xml + 1) == '/')
 							p->datafunc(p->data, data, i);
 					}
 				}
